
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How to Use Streamline Task?";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<style>
    ul {
        list-style-type: square;
        font-family: Arial;
        font-size: 15px;
        text-align: justify
    }
</style>

<p>
    In this web application, we allow users to create, view, edit, and delete tasks created by them.
    This is a tool that allows you to list the tasks you need to complete in a clear form.
</p>
<br />
<br />

<h2><u>TIPS !</u></h2>
<br />
<p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 22px;">Create</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        Users can create many tasks according to their own needs. It will require users to choose the
        completion time and date of the task, so users can also record the tasks that need to be done
        in the next few days in advance to prevent forgetting them later.
    </li>
    <li>
        Users can add descriptions to tasks. Sometimes just a simple task name can make users confused
        or forget what they should do, so the description column plays its role.
    </li>
</ul>
<p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 22px;">View</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        Users can browse all existing tasks they have added, including deadlines and task descriptions,
        reminding them when and how to complete the task.
    </li>
    <li>
        Users can see the current total number of tasks and the number of completed tasks, which easily
        helps to sort out the urgency of time.
    </li>
</ul>
<p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 22px;">Delete</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        Users can delete completed tasks to maintain the cleanliness of the page.
    </li>
    <li>
        Users can delete tasks that have been entered incorrectly or cancelled to prevent confusion.
    </li>
</ul>
<p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 22px;">Checked</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        When the user completes the task, click the checkbox to prove that it has been completed.
        Users can clearly see which tasks have been completed and which tasks are not yet completed.
    </li>
    <li>
        Under the task list bar, the system will display the number of completed tasks based on the
        number of checked items in the user's checkbox.
    </li>
</ul>

<br />
<br />
